  - [1mComplexity:[0m moderate.

  [1mMy recommendation: A, borrowing exactly one thing from C[0m — store a versioned envelope ([38;5;153mv[39m, [38;5;153muserId[39m, [38;5;153msource[39m, [38;5;153mcreatedAt[39m)
  rather than a bare string, and keep the accessor returning just the id.

  The reason for A over B is your own constraint: "other forms will need it later too" is the sentence that makes the
  boundary worth having now, when there are zero call sites to migrate instead of several. The reason for borrowing from
  C rather than taking it whole is that "not sure yet" about the backend makes an unversioned bare string the one
  genuinely expensive thing to undo — a raw [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m string with no version tag gives you no safe way to detect and
  migrate old values later, and that costs one extra field today. The rest of C — [38;5;153mlastLoginAt[39m, reconciliation logic — is
  speculative until you know whether a server id is coming, so I'd leave it out under YAGNI.

  Does this shortlist look right before I take the recommendation into a sectioned design?

